<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.2.0:
* Fixed endless recursion when loading from a stream
* Fixed file handles not being released
* Prices are written culture-invariant (prices &gt;= 1000 were corrupted)
* Status, condition, item type and sub condition are written as BrickStore codes
* Currency and BrickLinkChangelogId are read/written as attributes of &lt;Inventory&gt;
* All supported item fields survive save/load; default values and empty elements are no longer written
* New item properties Reserved, Cost, TotalWeight, MarkerText and MarkerColor
* Elements not interpreted by the library (e.g. DifferenceBaseValues, GuiState) are kept in AdditionalElements and written back unchanged
* External entities are never resolved when loading
* Breaking: synchronous Load/Save throw the original exception instead of AggregateException; missing optional text elements load as null
1.0.0: Initial version</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <AssemblyVersion>1.2.0</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>1.2.0</FileVersion>
    <AssemblyName>BrickStoreSharp</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>BrickStoreSharp</PackageId>
    <Authors>Stephan Stapel</Authors>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/stephanstapel/BrickStoreSharp</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/stephanstapel/BrickStoreSharp</RepositoryUrl>
    <Description>BrickStoreSharp is a .NET Standard library designed for handling BrickStore inventory files with ease and efficiency. This library allows users to read and write BrickStore inventory files (https://github.com/rgriebl/brickstore), providing a streamlined approach for managing and manipulating LEGO brick inventories. Features
* Read and write BrickStore inventory files
* Compatible with .NET Standard 2.0
* Simple and intuitive API

Find more about the library here:
https://github.com/stephanstapel/BrickStoreSharp</Description>
    <IncludeSymbols>True</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <Version>1.2.0</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
